### Description

See [simple repro repo](https://github.com/billybraga/DotnetEnumerableServiceBug/blob/main/DotnetEnumerableServiceBug/Program.cs).

Basically, in dotnet 6 preview5, getting IEnumerable<> service (to get all implementations) is broken if service provider validates on build because slots are not always determined the same way and the validate step builds call site cache differently.

This snippet will throw:

```csharp
var services = new ServiceCollection();
services.AddSingleton<ICustomService, CustomService1>();
services.AddSingleton<ICustomService, CustomService2>();
services.AddSingleton<ICustomService, CustomService3>();
services.AddSingleton<ICustomService, CustomService4>();
services.AddSingleton<ICustomService, CustomService5>();
var serviceProvider = services.BuildServiceProvider(
    new ServiceProviderOptions
    {
        ValidateOnBuild = true
    }
);
var customServices = serviceProvider
    .GetService<IEnumerable<ICustomService>>()
    .ToArray()
// Index 1 should be CustomService2 but instead we get 5
if (customServices[1] is CustomService5 && customServices[4] is CustomService5)
{
    throw new Exception(
        "This is not right"
    );
}
```

### Configuration

dotnet 6 preview 5.21301.5

### Regression?

Yes

### Other information

I think this is the code that caused the bug : https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/bb2d2c45410b9407a9657df7f5ca113bced53a43#diff-12fe7d127bc25efffaedd4b50d0b12792aa7c236e855d782c127424fa2f9dbb0

The problem is maybe that `descriptors.GetSlot()` should be used here : https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/v6.0.0-preview.5.21301.5/src/libraries/Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection/src/ServiceLookup/CallSiteFactory.cs#L176
